<title>BELGIUM: EU starts probe into German aid to Infraleuna.</title>
<headline>EU starts probe into German aid to Infraleuna.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Wednedsay it had started a probe into financial aid amounting to 532.5 million Europan currency units in favour of Infraleuna Infrastrukur- und Service GmBH.</p>
<p>The former East German company supplies services to chemical companies in the eastern city of Leuna.  </p>
<p>The Commission said in a statement it had &quot;serious doubts&quot; about whether the aid could be allowed under Eurorpean Union laws, saying it was concerned that the amount could rise above that allowed for former East German companies.</p>
<p>Leuna is jointly owned by Germany's Linde AG and Belgium's Domo Group, with 49 percent in the public sector.</p>
